<title>USA: New York State ends FY 1997 with huge surplus.</title>
<headline>New York State ends FY 1997 with huge surplus.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York State Comptroller said Tuesday the state ended its 1997 fiscal year on April 1 with a $1.85 billion surplus, largely due to surging profits at Wall Street banks and brokerages.</p>
<p>Further, H. Carl McCall, in prepared remarks, noted that most of this huge sum was available for the state's new 1998 fiscal year.</p>
</text>
